 "raw_reply": "{\"item\": \"S441-013\", \"clauses\": {\"give\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F05\", \"template\": \"What {unit_label} comes right after {v}?\", \"reasoning\": \"The sequence question asks the learner to name the next unit in the sequence, which is the act of giving the units in order. F05 with unit_label drawn from the two sequence units produces it.\"}, \"days_of_the_week\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F05\", \"template\": \"What {unit_label} comes right after {v}?\", \"reasoning\": \"unit_label can be day of the week and v draws from reference_name, whose printed values include the seven day names, so F05 produces day-of-the-week items.\"}, \"months_of_the_year\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F05\", \"template\": \"What {unit_label} comes right after {v}?\", \"reasoning\": \"unit_label can be month of the year and v draws from reference_name, whose printed values include the twelve month names, so F05 produces month-of-the-year items.\"}, \"correct_order\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F06\", \"template\": \"What {unit_label} comes right before {v}?\", \"reasoning\": \"The before question tests the position of a unit relative to its neighbour, which is the correct order property. F06 produces it for both unit values.\"}}, \"failing_families\": [\"F03\", \"F05\", \"F06\"], \"failing_templates\": [\"The {elapsed_label} is the number of days or weeks that have passed.\", \"What {unit_label} comes right after {v}?\", \"What {unit_label} comes right before {v}?\"], \"overall\": \"FAIL\", \"reasoning\": \"F03 is printed as a hint and its slot elapsed_label is filled only from nested text of F02, whose sole printed value is the gate word for elapsed (how much time has passed). The joined sentence is grammatically broken and makes an incorrect statement, and it introduces the elapsed concept of days or weeks passing, which this lc does not teach and which the family's own vocabulary gate excludes. F05 and F06 fail because unit_label is derived from unit and v is derived from reference_name, and value_derivations is empty with no link between them. The domains therefore allow a question that names one unit (day of the week or month of the year) and asks about a reference name from the other unit, which is a wrong question for the learner. F07 (the keyed answer) depends on F05 and F06 for its consistency and is not separately at fault. F08 (distractors) passes: its members are plausible wrong choices from the generator's own list, and the mixed units are not a wrong statement by themselves.\"}",
